/// ### What it does
/// Checks for `set_len()` call that creates `Vec` with uninitialized elements.
/// This is commonly caused by calling `set_len()` right after allocating or
/// reserving a buffer with `new()`, `default()`, `with_capacity()`, or `reserve()`.
